 * console.log(user.role); // 'super_admin'
 */
export async function login(email, password) {
  // ...
}
```

### 5.3 Inline Comments (EXPLAIN WHY, NOT WHAT)

Complex logic MUST have inline comments explaining the *why*:

```javascript
// ❌ WRONG (explains what, not why)
const token = authHeader.split(' ')[1]; // Extract token from header

// ✅ CORRECT (explains why)
// Check Bearer header first (for Swagger/Postman) before falling back to cookies.
// This allows both frontend (cookie-based) and API testing tools (header-based) to work.
const authHeader = req.headers.authorization;
if (authHeader && authHeader.startsWith('Bearer ')) {
  token = authHeader.split(' ')[1];
}
```

**Areas Requiring Detailed Comments:**
- Dynamic module resolution and hot-dropping.
- Cryptographic checks and signature verification.
- Dual-Auth flows and cookie handling.
- URL routing and deep linking logic.
- Cache invalidation strategies.
- Error recovery and retry logic.

