## 9. Deployment & DevOps

### 9.1 Environment Configuration

**REQUIRED:**
- `.env.example` — Template with all required variables (no secrets).
- `.env` (local) — Actual secrets for development (NEVER commit).
- Environment variables (production) — Injected at runtime.

### 9.2 Docker & Containerization

**REQUIRED:**
- Provide `Dockerfile` for both frontend and backend.
- Use multi-stage builds to minimize image size.
- Example:
  ```dockerfile
  FROM node:18-alpine AS builder
  WORKDIR /app
  COPY package*.json ./
  RUN npm ci
  COPY . .
  RUN npm run build
  
  FROM node:18-alpine
  WORKDIR /app
  COPY --from=builder /app/dist ./dist
  COPY --from=builder /app/node_modules ./node_modules
  EXPOSE 4001
  CMD ["node", "src/server.js"]
  ```

### 9.3 CI/CD Pipeline

**REQUIRED:**
- Automated tests on every commit.
- Automated linting and code quality checks.
- Automated builds and deployments.
- Example (GitHub Actions):
  ```yaml
  name: CI/CD
  on: [push, pull_request]
  jobs:
    test:
      runs-on: ubuntu-latest
      steps:
        - uses: actions/checkout@v3
        - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        - run: npm ci
        - run: npm run lint
        - run: npm test
        - run: npm run build
  ```

